2025-03-14 19:08:02,782 - DEBUG - Engine result: qas=[QA(question='What is differential geometry?', answer='Differential geometry is a mathematical discipline that studies the geometry of smooth shapes and smooth spaces, also known as smooth manifolds. It uses techniques from single variable calculus, vector calculus, linear algebra, and multilinear algebra.'), QA(question="How does differential geometry relate to Einstein's general theory of relativity?", answer="Differential geometry is the language used to express Einstein's general theory of relativity. According to the theory, the universe is a smooth manifold equipped with a pseudo-Riemannian metric, describing the curvature of spacetime."), QA(question='What are some applications of differential geometry outside of physics?', answer='Outside physics, differential geometry finds applications in chemistry, economics, engineering, control theory, computer graphics, computer vision, and recently in machine learning.'), QA(question="What was the significance of Gauss's work in differential geometry?", answer="Gauss's work is deemed the single most important in the history of differential geometry. He introduced concepts like the Gauss map, Gaussian curvature, first and second fundamental forms, and proved the Theorema Egregium, showing the intrinsic nature of Gaussian curvature."), QA(question='What are Riemannian manifolds?', answer='Riemannian manifolds are smooth manifolds with a Riemannian metric, which is a concept of distance expressed by a smooth positive definite symmetric bilinear form defined on the tangent space at each point. They generalize Euclidean geometry to non-flat spaces that resemble Euclidean space at each point infinitesimally.')]
